WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.267
[music playing]

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.702
You guys ready?

00:00:02.769 --> 00:00:03.503
Yeah.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:06.206
There you go, little buddy.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.006
Dump them out.

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:10.110
It's so cute.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:11.211
Just stay calm.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.512
Let him go, let him go.

00:00:12.579 --> 00:00:15.014
He wants to go to
the willow line.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:18.118
Run, run to the forest.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:20.920
Porcupine Chase was a lot
of fun, a lot more fun

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.623
having the kids with me out here
because for the kids, it's fun.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:25.592
So that makes it
real fun for me.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:26.926
Run away, little porcupine.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.995
It's so little.

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.930
And cute.

00:00:30.997 --> 00:00:33.900
OK, we got the
porcupine out of there.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.636
And now we have
to accept the house.

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.872
Yeah, let's put some
sheet iron on the cabin.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.607
That way, the next
porcupine come along

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.075
can't just eat it up.

00:00:42.142 --> 00:00:47.280
[music playing]

00:00:50.717 --> 00:00:52.085
OK.

00:00:52.152 --> 00:00:55.388
Let's push against it like that.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.756
Got rid of the
porcupine, now I want

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:59.726
to make sure any other
porcupine that come up

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:02.162
can't chew on the cabin
like this one was doing.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:03.897
Don't drop it on your toes.

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:05.865
Oh, we're going to
put it right here?

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.101
Yeah, you can just
go all the way down.

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:12.972
[hammering]

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:13.907
There you go.

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:15.108
And then at the bottom.

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.310
Oh yeah.

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:19.546
Pound it all the way in.

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:21.381
There you go, you got it.

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:27.320
Oh, they're right there.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:29.489
This is the best way for
me to bond with my children

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.925
because they learn a
lot and it's hands on.

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:34.060
And sometimes I
think in the city,

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.262
they can almost become
like they don't need me.

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:37.897
They have everything at hand.

00:01:37.964 --> 00:01:39.866
Do you think a porcupine
can climb up this medal?

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:40.700
Mm-mm.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.302
No way.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:43.970
When they're out here
in the environment,

00:01:44.037 --> 00:01:45.472
they can sense the danger.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:49.242
And they're relying on me 100%
so they kind of become sponges.

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.844
They soak in all the
knowledge real quick

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:53.279
when we're in an environment
like this traveling.

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:54.881
And that's how they learn.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:56.316
Get them out in the field.

00:01:56.382 --> 00:01:58.284
Gonna do the last one.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:01:59.419
And expose them to it.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:02.622
And they learn the right
way to survive out here.

00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.057
[hammering]

00:02:04.123 --> 00:02:06.893
There you go.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:08.728
I'm real proud of you guys.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.564
We came in, we did our business.

00:02:11.631 --> 00:02:14.033
When we leave, we
leave a better place.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:14.834
I'm tired.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.870
Yeah, me too.

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:19.572
Let's go get some rest.

00:02:19.639 --> 00:02:20.974
No quills in the den.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.076
[music playing]

